ful in terms of if you're  playing somebody who's really existed  yeah of course you can watch interviews  you can listen to their voice  there's something  that a photograph can capture  that tells you a lot about somebody and  with houston it was very much his hands  his fingers were always in the most  beautiful position  yes  i have this feeling like he sort of  curated his life you know he liked to  have camera crews around he started  filming everything so there's lots of  footage of him  i had my hair darkened to play him  because he had dark hair so when we went  back from lockdown i went back to la i  thought at first we were told you know  we're shutting down for two weeks  [Laughter]  but the first thing i did was after once  i realized  it wasn't gonna be quick that we went  back i i i wanted to try and lighten my  hair because i it's odd when you're you  but you don't look like you it's fine if  you're working on something but when i  was just off i so i went to the  supermarket and i got some  hair lightener i just bought it off the  shelf i thought this will do  my hair totally  peroxide like yellow white you know and  this like  [ __ ]  had a nightmare that they might call me  back to work you know like soon and i  would be turning back out with this like  orangey white hair oh my god  [Music]  our costume designer jerry anna was  amazing at teaching me how to make the  dresses that i am seen making in the  show i can't learn to be a  amazing dressmaker in you know a few  months so  what we did is we took each  each time you see me draping i just  learned  how to make those dresses like how you  would drape them and also just the act  of pinning i had to look like i knew  what i was doing i didn't want my hands  to sort of give me away you know he was  so  graceful and and i loved all the images  of him and he was always sort of behind  one of his models or whoever he was  draping and  look he was really  focused in the mirror and he had this he  had